[ ] Retire the homed Darrion account =retire-homed $Erased and verified 2026-10-21 (see Log). Left: drop the stale Darrion entry from group data (sudo gpasswd -d Darrion data), remove that account's ssh key from GitHub if it was added, and unlink that desktop in Signal. The drive stays in its enclosure until =desktop-install moves it.$ +human ^2026-10-21T00:04 <homed-inventory #01a15bc6-5a28-7232-9260-740b2519e82d
[ ] Write the desktop mkosi profile =desktop-profile $Base plus hardware selection (Intel and NVIDIA), from the sort. Built and booted in a VM before it touches hardware. Its package list is the sort's base and hardware rows (pacman, plus AUR built in the image); chezmoi keeps only user-level tools. Two checks carried from the sort: the Brother scanner's model (which AUR driver, if any) and whether Flatpak Steam uses the host gamemode. Brother: a DS-620, so libsane-dsseries built from Brother's package; brscan5 dropped.$ ^2026-10-21T00:04 <desktop-sort <desktop-list-home #01a15bc6-5a3f-7a32-b39e-7e9bf807954e
[ ] Mount /home and /data from their own disks =desktop-mounts $repart lays out only the boot disk; the other two become mount units. /data keeps group data, setgid and default ACLs.$ ^2026-10-21T00:04 <desktop-profile #01a15bc6-5a48-75d1-a68b-cb281ca65d2c
[ ] Install the desktop profile on the 1 TB NVMe beside Arch =desktop-install $Darrion, 2026-10-21: install while the drive is still in its USB enclosure, then move it. 1) Test the built image in a VM from the image file. 2) Write it to the drive from Arch, addressed as /dev/disk/by-id/usb-Best_Buy_NS-PCNVMEHDE_-C__4834500000003539-0:0, confirmed before writing (four NVMe disks once it is inside). 3) Boot the desktop from the USB drive once. 4) Move it into the free M.2 slot (a standard M.2 NVMe; the desktop has no SATA disks to lose) and boot from there. Arch stays untouched; the boot menu picks. Secure Boot is already on with Darrion's own keys (bootctl: enabled (user), likely sbctl): either add personal-os's db certificate beside them or sign the desktop image with the sbctl keys; decide at this step.$ +human ^2026-10-21T00:20 <desktop-profile #01a15bd4-c3df-7782-bc59-31be2e0f11a2
[ ] Wipe the Arch root disk once personal-os holds up =wipe-arch $nvme2n1 (WD_BLACK SN850X) is freed for data. What holds up means is agreed with Darrion before the wipe; the wipe is a disk write that needs Darrion's explicit go. At the same time, remove chezmoi's bootstrap-paru hook, which only Arch-with-pacman machines use.$ +human ^2026-10-21T00:20 <desktop-install #01a15bd4-c3e8-7d72-91f4-8697fb1281c2
